at it sounds like this:\n              [‘histri/ Oo. The first part of the word geography may be pronounced as one or two syllables:\n                          Ooo or                    Many  speakers do not pronounce the second syllable in\n               mathematics, so it sounds like this:            oOo.\n    C  |  852 If we combine  the various endings  in this unit and Unit 30, we can get ‘families’ of words with\n              moving   stress patterns. Listen to these examples.\n              photograph     photography    photographic\n              economy       economics       economical\n              National       nationality    nationalise     nationalisation\n              civil         civility        civilise        civilisation\n\n\n    70\n                 English Pronunciation in Use", "char_count": 2746, "mean_conf": 86.88, "word_count": 372, "words": [{"text": "stress", "x0": 293, "y0": 375, "x1": 394, "y1": 400, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "is", "x0": 410, "y0": 367, "x1": 436, "y1": 400, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "placed", "x0": 452, "y0": 364, "x1": 574, "y1": 410, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "on", "x0": 590, "y0": 378, "x1": 638, "y1": 401, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "the", "x0": 652, "y0": 365, "x1": 710, "y1": 402, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "syllable", "x0": 726, "y0": 365, "x1": 868, "y1": 411, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "two", "x0": 882, "y0": 376, "x1": 956, "y1": 403, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "from", "x0": 971, "y0": 366, "x1": 1064, "y1": 403, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "the", "x0": 1079, "y0": 367, "x1": 1137, "y1": 403, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "end.", "x0": 1152, "y0": 367, "x1": 1231, "y1": 403, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "Listen", "x0": 1247, "y0": 369, "x1": 1362, "y1": 404, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "to", "x0": 1377, "y0": 378, "x1": 1415, "y1": 404, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "these", "x0": 1430, "y0": 3